| Connect Bitbucket and its set-up (#3785): the **Connect Bitbucket** sheet (Mac) and dialog (web): an Atlassian API token with its account's email, or a repository, project or workspace access token with none, checked by the host with Bitbucket Cloud (`GET /2.0/user`, Basic or Bearer) and kept in its store (`connections.Bitbucket`); its row on Your Connectors says **bitbucket.org · Token**, with **Disconnect**. A folder whose remote is on bitbucket.org gets Tasks (**Bitbucket issues**), Code review (**Bitbucket pull requests**) and CI (**Bitbucket checks**, the main branch's statuses) from the connection, each proved by one read, and the bitbucket server's events turned on once; the bitbucket server reads the connection; the connection's nickname is the viewer's Bitbucket login in the control plane's people when Settings ▸ Account gives none (#3853) | Mac, web | built, walked on scratch with a fake Bitbucket | — | 2026-11-07, against a fake Bitbucket (`TestConnectingBitbucketWithAToken`, `TestABitbucketFoldersConnectorSetUp`, `Go/internal/bitbucketmcp/setup_test.go`), and walked on a scratch Mac window and web page with a fake Bitbucket API on loopback (`BITBUCKET_API_URL`, `Web/test/walk/bitbucket3785.mjs`): a wrong token, a token that connects, and the three slots read | `Go/internal/connections/bitbucket.go`, `Go/internal/agentsd/connectorsetup.go`, `Go/internal/bitbucketmcp/setup.go`, `App/Sources/MCPServers/ConnectTokenSheet.swift` (the one token sheet since #3802), `Web/src/views/ConnectorSetup.tsx` | not yet on a real workspace (Alex's test, #3771): Bitbucket Cloud has no local container, and whether `GET /2.0/user` names a repository, project or workspace access token's bot is unproven; the row cannot say an API token's end, which Bitbucket does not give; the Remote: by design (tier mac+web) |
